Explain corrosion through electrochemistry, transport, local structure, and actual exposure (@metal-corrosion: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Environmental-Degradation-of-Materials-NPTEL.lingua#r_06WSRAYJJKWNTT146BKY5BN4QQ", #source "../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T", #source "../sources/Steels-Structure-Properties-and-Design.lingua#r_5CB9R75MR8424M7VJ5Y33FY0QF", #source "../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Contact-friction-wear-and-tribological-system-evidence.lingua#r_54DD7QV8DEW4WB6QDHYA4NXZJQ") { r_761808KRW6H2NDYPQT1JD8NCKC
**Read:** [Environmental Degradation of Materials — Kallol Mondal, NPTEL](../sources/Environmental-Degradation-of-Materials-NPTEL.lingua#r_06WSRAYJJKWNTT146BKY5BN4QQ), the complete relevant theory and examples, followed by full primary methods; [Aluminium Automotive Manual — European Aluminium and collaborators](../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T), entire applicable material, surface, joining, and service cases; [Steels: Structure, Properties, and Design — Bhadeshia and Honeycombe](../sources/Steels-Structure-Properties-and-Design.lingua#r_5CB9R75MR8424M7VJ5Y33FY0QF), complete stainless/embrittlement and primary evidence, when available; [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC), the full environment/mechanism and failure context.

Corrosion behavior depends on reaction potentials and rates, transport, surface films, local chemistry, microstructure, geometry, mechanical state, and exposure history. General loss, localized attack, galvanic effects, environmentally assisted cracking, and high-temperature reactions require different evidence and models.

Reuse Nernst, electrode kinetics, transport, phase/chemistry, and surface/structure knowledge. A nominal alloy designation or passive appearance does not establish behavior in every environment. Local segregation, inclusions, interfaces, weld regions, stress, deposits, flow, and changing chemistry can control a failure that a bulk average misses.

Define exposure/test conditions, preparation, time, electrochemical reference/resistance treatment, sampling, and the measured damage criterion. An accelerated test or a polarization result does not automatically predict all service times or mechanisms. Compare independent field/laboratory evidence and appropriate uncertainty.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete alloy/environment study with original electrochemical/structural and damage methods. Independently reproduce a representative charge/loss or transport/kinetic calculation, compare mechanisms, and validate against changed conditions. Defend an alternative material, surface, design, or operating arrangement using the whole service/maintenance account. The later dedicated corrosion/protection trail deepens specialized methods while reusing these common explanations.

**Continue:** [Treat wear as behavior of a contact system with material and environmental history](Contact-friction-wear-and-tribological-system-evidence.lingua#r_54DD7QV8DEW4WB6QDHYA4NXZJQ).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
